From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: paint the external shell's caption over the whole caption height

Purpose: remove the grey line between a themed caption and the window body.
The caption geometry ends one pixel above SM_CYCAPTION, which is right for
placing the buttons, the icon and the title, but the caption image was also
painted only that high. The row below kept the window colour, while XP
stretches the caption image over it. Painting the background over the full
height makes the caption of a restored folder window equal the reference XP
machine's in its unstretched part, with buttons and title unchanged.

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/window.c b/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
index 1a230f2..e20e9d6 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/window.c
@@ -421,6 +421,10 @@ BOOL WINAPI Win4WineDrawNonClient(HWND hwnd, HDC target)
     border_y = GetSystemMetrics(style & WS_THICKFRAME ? SM_CYFRAME : SM_CYDLGFRAME);
     caption_height = GetSystemMetrics(SM_CYCAPTION) - 1;
     themed_caption_geometry(hwnd, theme, &caption, buttons);
+    /* The buttons and title are placed against the raw caption height, but XP
+     * stretches the caption image over the whole SM_CYCAPTION, including the
+     * row that would otherwise stay in the window colour above the client. */
+    caption.bottom = max(caption.bottom, min(border_y + GetSystemMetrics(SM_CYCAPTION), client.top));
     if (!target) caption_region_update(hwnd, theme, &caption, maximized);
     DrawThemeBackground(theme, dc, maximized ? WP_MAXCAPTION : WP_CAPTION, state, &caption, NULL);
     part = window; part.top = caption.bottom; part.right = border_x;
